  12 of 12 stay profitable across 95%+ of the ensemble.

  These strategies were evolved on real data and never saw a synthetic bar,
  so they cannot have gamed the generator — the ensemble can only take money
  from them. A large drop means the strategy was living on the absence of
  the dead.

  READ A SMALL DROP WITH CARE. Measured 2026-09-12: the crash-buying
  survivors took only 8-18% damage, and not because they dodged the
  synthetic failures — 23.5% of their entries landed in them, slightly MORE
  than the 19.9% those names make up of the panel. They survived because a
  60-day holding cap and an ATR stop exit a dying company at -10 or -20%
  long before it reaches zero.

  That is only true while the decline is smooth enough for a stop to fill,
  and these paths are. Real bankruptcies gap: the position opens through the
  stop with no liquidity behind it, which is a limitation this project already
  documents for live trading and which the generator under-represents. The
  honest reading is that this ensemble tests slow death well and sudden death
  badly.
